{"id": "EUVD-2026-103561", "enisaUuid": "e215ffde-9b60-337e-9a62-a210591427ec", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Fix divide-by-zero in btf_struct_walk()\n\nWhen an access goes past the struct and the last member is a flexible\narray, btf_struct_walk() folds the offset back into a single element with\n(off - moff) % t->size, but never checks that the element type has a size.\n\nBTF takes an empty struct, so this in program BTF\n\n\t/* event could be empty */\n\tstruct event {\n #ifdef HAVE_TIMESTAMP\n\t\t__u64 ts;\n #endif\n\t};\n\n\tstruct batch {\n\t\tint nr;\n\t\tstruct event events[];\n\t};\n\ndivides by zero at prog load time. Getting there needs a PTR_TO_BTF_ID that\nis not MEM_ALLOC, e.g. a plain read of a local kptr stashed in a map from a\nsleepable program.\n\nOops: divide error: 0000 [#1] SMP KASAN PTI\nRIP: 0010:btf_struct_walk+0x53f/0x1570\nCall Trace:\n <TASK>\n btf_struct_access+0x42a/0xcd0\n check_ptr_to_btf_access+0x4dc/0x1160\n check_mem_access+0x3a45/0x8740\n check_load_mem+0x36a/0xd10\n do_check_common+0x3ef0/0xb210\n bpf_check+0x6d3b/0x8580\n bpf_prog_load+0xf7c/0x2720\n __sys_bpf+0xa83/0x3690\n __x64_sys_bpf+0xc7/0x150\n x64_sys_call+0x1f3f/0x27e0\n do_syscall_64+0xe5/0x610\n entry_SYSCALL_64_after_hwframe+0x76/0x7e\n </TASK>\n\nReject a zero-sized element type. The fixed array path in the same function\nalready bails out on the same thing:\n\n\tbtf_struct_walk()\n\t...\n\t\t/* skip empty array */\n\t\tif (moff == mtrue_end)\n\t\t\tcontinue;\n\n\t\tmsize /= total_nelems;", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:16", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ea3820937f8022e044c41c6e95c84b02741b45f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/172756f02663ad45c889c001c1a8cb4082a01a05", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/934e9ba9f8d05656a48624710be67ca4dc8482e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63af086cb5fa6f72fd924f86bea4c2194da663a2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8eb4cd72daad3a9ee63d2281bbdd16ce6d9406b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b8fa56722e9c43bcd59c51fe4c7edd5f4158a11b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b0b3dc66529676228cb938cbcad66920f735c223"], "aliases": ["GHSA-p98x-gg62-cxq2", "CVE-2026-98647"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0079cbbc-cd8f-37b5-b832-6d51b34004d2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c5f8a1008a121e4c6b24af211034e24b0b63081 <b8fa56722e9c43bcd59c51fe4c7edd5f4158a11b"}, {"id": "0dc8f103-5034-3771-9278-d452828d0355", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "0edc3f6a-9b05-3896-a301-7a0758673a7a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c5f8a1008a121e4c6b24af211034e24b0b63081 <b0b3dc66529676228cb938cbcad66920f735c223"}, {"id": "273ecb36-83d3-3e16-82b7-21fa86edc54e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c5f8a1008a121e4c6b24af211034e24b0b63081 <1ea3820937f8022e044c41c6e95c84b02741b45f"}, {"id": "334b5a13-6830-371e-aa06-311d098fd690", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "38bebf46-0611-3730-ad07-ed26dff732d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b86555d-7593-39c2-8660-6e9638df6edb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "47fd6fec-4882-3943-b663-53692a145f14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "535363b7-8100-3f82-99ef-114a14f35ffa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "9c5f8a1008a121e4c6b24af211034e24b0b63081 <172756f02663ad45c889c001c1a8cb4082a01a05"}, {"id": "6f3f80a7-bff2-3502-ae6f-f16ebff08c5b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "produ